From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] video: say where the picture is at the end of the pipe

Everything this driver reports about timing is taken before the video
post-processor, so it cannot see how many frames the Dolby Vision core and the
scaler hold - which is the depth between an offset measured in the player and the
one arriving at the connector.

Add one node sampled in a single go with interrupts off: the CLOCK_MONOTONIC base
DRM timestamps vblanks on, the encoder's frame count, the line it is putting out
now, and the post-processor CRC where that exists. Read one at a time they say
nothing about each other.

Read-only, measurement only. Nothing in the driver acts on it.

--- a/drivers/media/video_sink/video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/video_sink/video.c
@@ -10802,6 +10802,54 @@
 	return strnlen(buf, count);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Where the picture actually is, at the far end of the pipe.
+ *
+ * Everything else this driver reports about timing is taken before the video
+ * post-processor: pts_video is stamped from the video layer, so it says nothing
+ * about how many frames the Dolby Vision core and the scaler hold, and that
+ * depth is exactly what stands between a measured offset and the one arriving at
+ * the connector.
+ *
+ * Three readings, taken with interrupts off because read one at a time they say
+ * nothing about each other, which is the only reason to have them:
+ *
+ *   mono   CLOCK_MONOTONIC, the base DRM timestamps vblanks on, so an audio
+ *          position read beside this can be subtracted from it
+ *   vsync  frames the encoder has begun since boot. Not vsync_cnt[], which
+ *          counts only the interrupts that had to be dropped and so reads zero
+ *          on a healthy box
+ *   line   which line of the current frame the encoder is putting out now,
+ *          i.e. how far into the frame this reading was taken
+ *   crc    of the frame the post-processor produced, when vpp_crc is enabled.
+ *          Always zero on this SoC: vpp_crc_check() gates the whole read on
+ *          cpu_after_eq(SM1) and g12b is earlier, so the field is carried for
+ *          the parts that have it rather than for this one. Without it the
+ *          reading places the output in time but cannot say which frame is in
+ *          it, which leaves the pipeline depth a constant to be measured once
+ *          from outside rather than something this node can answer.
+ *
+ * Read-only, and reads a register the vsync path already reads every frame.
+ */
+static ssize_t av_probe_show
+	(struct class *cla,
+	struct class_attribute *attr,
+	char *buf)
+{
+	unsigned long flags;
+	u32 vsync, line;
+	u64 mono;
+
+	local_irq_save(flags);
+	mono = ktime_get_ns();
+	vsync = vsync_count;
+	line = get_cur_enc_line();
+	local_irq_restore(flags);
+
+	return snprintf(buf, 128, "mono %llu vsync %u line %u crc %x\n",
+		mono, vsync, line, vpp_crc_result);
+}
+
 static ssize_t vpp_crc_show
 	(struct class *cla,
 	struct class_attribute *attr,
@@ -13353,6 +13401,7 @@
 	       0664,
 	       path_select_show,
 	       path_select_store),
+	__ATTR_RO(av_probe),
 	__ATTR(vpp_crc,
 	       0664,
 	       vpp_crc_show,
